      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِخلى المَاشِيَةَ</span></b> , (inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِخْلَآءٌ</span>, TA,) said of
God, <i>He made</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَلًى</span> <i>to grow for the cattle.</i> (Lh,
K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also 1, in three places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اخلت</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَرْضُ</span> <i>The land became abundant in</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَلًى</span>. (JK,
S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [And hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اخلى</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>He uttered words,</i>
or <i>expressions, without any great meaning.</i> (Ham
p. 391.)

